# Holistic Component and Section Review

When the user asks to review, fix, improve, or implement a named UI part (for example “header”, “footer”, “sidebar”, “form”, “card”, “modal”, “nav”), do not treat it as a single isolated visual block.
Inspect and correct the full related surface area.

## Default Expansion Rule

Expand the request to include:

1. all variants of that part
2. all breakpoints
3. all interactive subparts
4. all states
5. all dependent behaviors and files

Example: “بررسی هدر” / “check the header” means review and fix at least:

- desktop header layout and spacing
- logo / brand treatment
- primary navigation
- secondary actions / CTAs
- mobile menu / hamburger / drawer / sheet
- open, close, escape, overlay, scroll-lock, and focus behavior for mobile nav
- active/current link states
- search UI if present or implied by the product/header pattern
- search open/close, suggestions, clear, empty, loading, and keyboard behavior if search exists
- auth/account menu, language switcher, theme toggle, notifications, or cart if present in that header system
- sticky/fixed behavior, shadow/border on scroll, z-index stacking
- accessibility: keyboard, focus-visible, aria-expanded, labels, landmarks
- responsive overflow, wrapping, and touch targets
- header interaction with page content (offset, overlap, focus not obscured)

## Common Surfaces and What They Include

### Header / Navbar
- brand, nav links, CTA, utilities
- mobile navigation and animation/transition
- search, account, locale, theme, notifications, cart if part of the same system
- sticky behavior, height, z-index, contrast over hero/media

### Footer
- link groups, legal links, social icons
- newsletter/form if present
- responsive stacking, spacing, contrast, focusable links
- metadata/copyright consistency

### Sidebar / Dashboard Nav
- collapsed/expanded states
- active item, nested items, mobile drawer equivalent
- keyboard and screen-reader labels
- content area offset and overflow

### Forms
- labels, validation, error text, helper text
- disabled/loading submit
- keyboard submit, autocomplete, input modes
- success/error summaries
- related dialogs or confirmations

### Cards / Lists / Tables
- empty/loading/error states
- responsive alternative layouts
- action menus, truncation, alignment
- row/card hover-focus behaviors

### Modal / Drawer / Popover / Dropdown
- trigger, open/close, overlay
- focus trap and restore
- escape and outside click according to pattern
- scroll lock and stacking context
- mobile sizing and keyboard handling

### Search
- input, submit/clear, keyboard enter
- results/suggestions/no-results/loading
- debounce and accessibility announcements when relevant
- integration with header/mobile nav when search lives there

## Review Procedure

When asked to review/fix a part:

1. Locate the main component and all related files (mobile menu, search, hooks, styles, tests, stories).
2. Map the full surface: subcomponents, breakpoints, states, and integrations.
3. Fix issues across that whole surface, not only the obvious desktop markup.
4. Verify keyboard use, responsive behavior, and state coverage.
5. Report what related areas were included in the review.

## Do Not Do This

- Do not only restyle the desktop bar and ignore mobile menu behavior.
- Do not ignore search/account/locale controls that belong to the same component system.
- Do not leave broken open/close, focus, overlay, or scroll-lock behavior.
- Do not declare a header/nav “done” if mobile navigation is incomplete.
- Do not invent unrelated product features, but do complete implied parts of the same UI system.

## Response Contract

When finishing such a task, briefly state:

- which related subparts were reviewed
- which breakpoints/states were covered
- what was fixed
- any remaining risks outside the current scope
